        - Output: :math:`(N, C, D, H, W)` or :math:`(C, D, H, W)` (same shape as input).

    Examples::

        >>> m = nn.FeatureAlphaDropout(p=0.2)
        >>> input = torch.randn(20, 16, 4, 32, 32)
        >>> output = m(input)

    .. _Self-Normalizing Neural Networks: https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.02515
